&lt;img src="https://res.infoq.com/news/2026/03/sbom-viktor-petersson/en/headerimage/generatedHeaderImage-1773839022229.jpg"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;In a talk at QCon London 2026, Viktor Petersson argued that software teams are running out of time to adopt SBOMs (Software Bills of Materials) due to pending legislative changes in both the US and Europe.&#xD;
&#xD;
He walked through the current regulatory landscape, spoke on the practical mechanics of generating high-quality SBOMs and on the emerging standards for distributing the resulting artefacts.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;i&gt;By Matt Saunders&lt;/i&gt;

&lt;img src="https://res.infoq.com/news/2026/03/sbom-viktor-petersson/en/headerimage/generatedHeaderImage-1773839022229.jpg"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;In a talk at QCon London 2026, Viktor Petersson argued that software teams are running out of time to adopt SBOMs (Software Bills of Materials) due to pending legislative changes in both the US and Europe.&#xD;
&#xD;
He walked through the current regulatory landscape, spoke on the practical mechanics of generating high-quality SBOMs and on the emerging standards for distributing the resulting artefacts.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;i&gt;By Matt Saunders&lt;/i&gt;
